SUMMARY:Josh Johnson's Comedy Band Camp LIVE at Kingsbury Hall (Fri)
DTSTAMP:20260821T033716Z
DTSTART:20260821T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout Josh Johnson\nJosh Johns
	on is one of the most exciting and intellectually sharp comedians working 
	today. With over 10 million followers across social media\, he was recentl
	y called “the funniest guy on the internet” by WIRED. An Emmy-nominated wr
	iter\, stand-up comedian\, actor\, and NAACP award-winner from Louisiana b
	y way of Chicago\, Johnson is currently a rotating host and correspondent 
	on Comedy Central’s Emmy & Peabody Award-winning program The Daily Show. \
	nJohnson is a prolific creator who releases weekly stand-up sets on his Yo
	uTube channel — content that has been viewed over half a billion times wor
	ldwide. In 2025 alone\, he released 38 hours of topical stand-up material 
	performed in front of live audiences. His comedy is intelligent\, timely\,
	 and deeply human — the kind that makes you laugh and think at the same ti
	me. \nThe Comedy Band Camp is Josh’s most ambitious live show yet — a uniq
	ue\, immersive comedy experience that he describes as “the camp experience
	 he never had\, so he made it for you.” This is not your typical stand-up 
	show. \nEvent Details\nDate: Friday\, August 21\, 2026 \nTime: 7:00 PM MDT
	 \nVenue: Kingsbury Hall\, 1395 Presidents Circle\, Salt Lake City\, UT 84
	112 \nPhone: (801) 581-7100 \nNote: A Saturday night show (Aug 22 at 8:30 
	PM) is also available. See separate listing. \nAbout Kingsbury Hall\nKings
	bury Hall is one of Salt Lake City’s most beloved and historic performance
	 venues\, located on the campus of the University of Utah at 1395 Presiden
	ts Circle. With a seating capacity of approximately 1\,900\, it offers an 
	intimate yet grand atmosphere perfect for a show as unique as Comedy Band 
	Camp. \nThe hall features excellent sightlines from virtually every seat\,
	 outstanding acoustics\, and a warm\, welcoming ambiance. Managed by UtahP
	resents\, Kingsbury Hall has hosted world-class performers across comedy\,
	 music\, and theater for decades. Parking is available in nearby Universit
	y of Utah parking structures\, and the venue is accessible via TRAX light 
	rail. \nWhat to Expect\nJosh Johnson’s Comedy Band Camp is unlike any come
	dy show you’ve seen before. Blending stand-up\, performance art\, and inte
	ractive elements\, the show creates a fully immersive experience that has 
	been wowing audiences across the country. Expect opening acts\, dancers (t
	he famous Flower Girls)\, and Josh’s signature brand of intelligent\, topi
	cal humor. \nJosh is known for crafting material that is specific to the c
	urrent moment — so every show feels fresh and relevant. His ability to wea
	ve together serious topics with genuine hilarity is unmatched in comedy ri
	ght now. Fans consistently describe his shows as life-changing experiences
	. \nDoors open approximately 45 minutes before showtime. Arrive early to f
	ind your seats and soak in the Kingsbury Hall atmosphere. \nTicket Informa
	tion\nPrice Range: Check venue for current pricing \nTickets are available
	 through the official Kingsbury Hall box office and authorized resale plat
	forms. Both Friday and Saturday shows are available — check both listings!
	 \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We
	 may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.
	com/event/josh-johnsons-comedy-band-camp-live-at-kingsbury-hall-fri/\n\nFr
	om Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/josh-johnsons-comedy-band-camp-live-at
	-kingsbury-hall-fri/
LOCATION:Kingsbury Hall Salt Lake City\, 1395 Presidents Circle\, Salt Lake
	 City\, Utah\, 84112\, United States
